    "details": "<p>The <strong>AdhigamAI Inter-College Hackathon</strong> is a multidisciplinary innovation challenge that brings together students, Artificial Intelligence, and real-world problem-solving. Participants develop practical technology-driven solutions for challenges across areas such as agriculture, defence, startups, citizen services, and road safety.</p>\n<p>The hackathon follows a <strong>two-round format</strong>&mdash;an online idea submission round followed by an offline Grand Finale, where shortlisted teams pitch their solutions and demonstrate working prototypes before industry experts and technical juries. The format encourages teams to build and refine their solutions in advance, making the finale focused on innovation, live demonstrations, expert interaction, and networking.</p>\n<p><strong>Rules&nbsp;</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Teams must have <strong>3&ndash;5 students</strong>, with one Team Leader; solo participation and joining multiple teams are not allowed. Hackathon_Rulebook</li>\n<li>Each team must choose <strong>one problem statement</strong> and submit an <strong>8&ndash;10 content-slide PPT/PDF</strong> in the required format before the deadline. Hackathon_RulebookHackathon_Rulebook</li>\n<li>All ideas, code, and prototypes must be <strong>original</strong>; plagiarism, fake demos, late submissions, or rule violations can lead to disqualification</li>\n</ul>",
